The last game which I finished today evolved a bit critical at one point.

It was the game where I had found a statue of the Wizard of Yendor in the
Valley and the petrified bones of an unlucky (or inattentive) adventurer.

I had decided to use seven of the second-hand (partly used) candles from
the bones and not to buy new ones at the lighting store in the mines.[*]

When I finally had everything including the kitch^H^H^H^H^H^H Book of the
Dead I went down to the Vibrating Square to perform the rite...

Lit the Candelabrum, ring the Bell, read the... - WTF - ...
"The runes appear scrambled.  You can't read them!"  It's cursed.
In the meantime the second-hand candles flicker low! (And the bell has
only one charge left since I accidentally applied it once.) Have to get
holy water out of my bag to uncurse the book. But summoned monsters are
surrounding me.

Finally the Book got uncursed, the Candelabrum lit again...

"You ring the Bell of Opening."
"The Bell of Opening issues an unsettling shrill sound..."
"Your candelabrum's candles' flames flicker low!"
<pray to Set!> (not #pray)
"What do you want to read? [B or ?*]"
"You begin to recite the runes.  The wraith misses.  You stop studying."
Etc. etc.; the monsters don't give me a minute to read that book, and
the candles' flame flickers low and lower - I really thought I spoiled
it.

Though finally the portal opened. Phew..

